# Semantic commits

Every commit message uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/):

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

Rules:

- Imperative, lowercase description; no trailing period
- `feat` / `fix` only when user-facing behavior changes
- Breaking change: `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer and/or `!` after type (`feat!: ...`)
- Changelog: `feat` → Added, `fix` → Fixed, `BREAKING CHANGE` → bump major

```
feat(mcp): add stream ticket for SSE auth
fix(send): reject unconfirmed approval hashes
docs: document dry-run mutations
```
